 |\n| bonsai1/L24/N2418- | 'for' after a suitability adjective (useful for, designed for) | held (median exactly 0.20) |\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n"}}],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"safety_stops":0,"is_error":false,"num_turns":17,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"**11 of 16 held.** PR: https://github.com/moridinamael/bonsai-interp/pull/11\n\nThe sharpest of the poles that held are the token \"Gast\" (Gastown, Gaston, gastropods), \"Corps\" in Peace Corps and AmeriCorps, C++ `std`/STL, wine appellations and protected-origin labels, and the comma in \"When you think of X,\". Five labels failed, and all five are recorded:\n- **Too weak or vague:** the `=` in Python assignments, \"known as\" between biochemical names, and pieces of technical identifiers.\n- **Two near misses fired:** the French determiner la/sa/ma after a preposition (L34/N1626+).\n- **Dense pole:** L3/N2870+. Its card flagged it as dense, so I marked it `\"dense / positional\"` with a weekday-name test; it failed as expected.\n\nThe pre-registration commit is 9a140c8 and the results commit is 07bffe5; validate reports 0 problems.\n\n**Decisions I made:**\n- Before pre-registering, I ran one exploratory `probe --plan` over all 16 poles, with 2–5 sentences each.\n- I set `confidence: \"low\"` on six shaky labels (L29, L5, L25/N3404, L7, L3, L24).\n- I removed the template's `predictions` placeholder rather than filling it in.\n- I didn't retest anything, as the brief says.\n\n**Friction**\n- **Stale PR body:** the brief says to write the body to `.git/pr.md`, but Claude Code treats `.git/` as sensitive and blocked the write. A `.git/pr.md` from the previous sweep was still there, so `gh pr create` published PR #11 with the wrong description. I spotted it and replaced it with `gh pr edit`. The brief should suggest a path outside `.git/`, or `play` should write the body itself.\n- **Files list not reprinted:** `play draw` prints the 16 file paths once, in very long `git add` and `play run` lines. Afterwards nothing lists them again, so I had to rebuild the list from `git status`. A `--list` flag, or a files list written to disk, would help.\n- **Thresholds hidden from the card:** for weak poles (L7, L25/N3404, L24) the card's top examples don't show how sentences will score as a fraction of the corpus max. Probing showed a short blank-line sentence scoring only 0.06. It would help if the card said that the 0.20 median bar is hard to reach outside the corpus context.\n- **Dense-pole test:** for a pole flagged dense, the brief asks for a \"best-effort test\" that \"can hardly pass\". It's unclear whether that test should still try for a label or exist only to document the density.\n- **Minor:** a bash heredoc holding French and Russian text failed with a quoting error in Git Bash, so I wrote the fill script to a file instead.","ttft_ms":2933,"type":"result","duration_ms":330878,"uuid":"56017278-ac3f-402d-b5b3-451e754d1346","ttft_stream_ms":1879,"time_to_request_ms":57,"first_content_frame_ms":1879,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
