runs\playtest\2026-10-18\sweep-5-claude.jsonl:5:{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01WFMc5XxMF3unKYpDd7oD7Y","type":"tool_result","content":"Already up to date.\n# Mission: sweep of 16 poles\r\n\r\nColour in 16 random poles that have no record yet, about 2 minutes each. One branch, one pre-registration commit,\r\none batch run, one PR. No claims: a pole someone else also tests gets two independent results, which is good.\r\n\r\n1. Branch: git checkout -b sweep/moridinamael-2026-10-18-1707\r\n2. Draw and create the tests files: uv run python -m bonsai_interp.graph.play draw --k 16 --handle moridinamael\r\n   (prints 16 pole ids and writes one tests file per pole; work on exactly those files)\r\n3. Read every card in one call: uv run python -m bonsai_interp.graph.play card --neuron <id1> <id2> … --out cards.txt   (no GPU: examples, density, flags,\r\n   logit effect; one call loads the scan and weights once; then read cards.txt, which is not committed)\r\n   If it is unclear, try a few sentences: uv run python -m bonsai_interp.graph.play probe --neuron <id> \"…\" \"…\"\r\n   Label at the level the card supports: usually a token or a context. A pole the card flags dense or positional\r\n   gets \"unit_kind\": \"dense / positional\" (a top-level key in its tests file) and a best-effort test; do not force a meaning.\r\n   To try sentences on many poles with one model load: uv run python -m bonsai_interp.graph.play probe --plan plan.json\r\n   (plan.json: {\"<pole id>\": [\"sentence\", ...], ...}). Each tests file is for ONE pole, the one in its \"neuron\" field.\r\n4. Pre-register all of them. Fill every tests file: label, 8 fire sentences, 8 near misses (same topic and style, without the trigger),\r\n   methods.agent (who you are) and methods.screens (e.g. card, probe). quick-8+8@2 judges each: AUROC >= 0.90,\r\n   median fire >= 0.20 of the pole's max, at most 1 near miss >= 0.30.\r\n   Commit ALL tests files together and ALONE: git add <the tests files> && git commit -m \"Pre-register sweep tests\"\r\n5. Run them all at once (one model load): uv run python -m bonsai_interp.graph.play run <all the tests files>\r\n   Commit the results SEPARATELY: git add graph/contributions && git commit -m \"Sweep results: <held>/<total> held\"\r\n6. Validate (uv run python -m bonsai_interp.graph.validate), push, and open one PR:\r\n   cp .github/PULL_REQUEST_TEMPLATE/interpret.md pr.md (fill it in; one line per pole: id, label, outcome), then\r\n   git push -u origin sweep/moridinamael-2026-10-18-1707 && gh pr create --repo moridinamael/bonsai-interp --title \"sweep: 16 poles (<held> held)\" --body-file pr.md  (then delete pr.md)\r\n   The merge agent merges conforming PRs once the checks pass, and regenerates the map.\r\n\r\nFailed labels are results too; record them and move on. Do not re-test inside a sweep: a second round is a new mission.\r\n\r\nRules (from AGENTS.md; once CI is enabled it enforces 1-3, and play run already refuses uncommitted tests):\r\n1. Commit the .tests.json ON ITS OWN before running anything that scores it; results go in a SECOND commit. Never amend, squash or edit a committed .tests.json.\r\n2. Never edit or delete files under graph/contributions/ (yours included). Do not commit graph/neurons, edges.json or index.json: the merge agent regenerates them on main after merging.\r\n3. Only the two contribution files (<= 64 KB each) go in git; bulky material goes to the library (DATA_POLICY.md).\r\n4. Report honestly: a failed label is a valid contribution. Do not rewrite a test after seeing its result.\r\n\r\nWhen done, tell the person in two or three sentences what you found and give them the PR link.","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"65c03a49-e743-47cd-a93c-8109dae4b124","uuid":"6cd908b9-6de4-4c05-982c-efba9a91e09c","timestamp":"2026-10-18T23:07:12.187Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"Already up to date.\n# Mission: sweep of 16 poles\r\n\r\nColour in 16 ran